+1 to this. I ran into the same thing using one fixed `opencode web --port 4096` server as a multi-project control room.

The confusing part is that the server/sessions are shared, but the Web sidebar project list appears to be per-browser/per-profile. Opening the same `http://127.0.0.1:4096` address in another browser gives a different/empty project sidebar, even though it is the same server.

One extra angle: it would be nice if this could also be preconfigured in `opencode.json`, distinct from `references`. References are useful as extra context directories, but they don't mean "show these as Web projects in the sidebar".

Example shape:

```jsonc
{
  "projects": {
    "tracker": "~/Sites/github/ctw-studio/tracker",
    "pure3d": "~/Sites/github/escience/Pure3D/Code/branch"
  }
}
```

Expected behavior: any browser/client connected to the same server hydrates the same recent/open/pinned Web projects from server-side state, optionally seeded by config.
